# WordPress Plugin to Clear Nginx Helper Cache on Plugin/Theme Changes

Here's a complete WordPress plugin that automatically clears the Nginx Helper cache whenever a plugin or theme is installed, updated, or changed:

```php
<?php
/*
Plugin Name: Nginx Helper Cache Buster
Description: Automatically clears Nginx Helper cache when plugins/themes are updated or changed
Version: 1.0
Author: Your Name
Author URI: https://yourwebsite.com
License: GPL2
*/

if (!defined('ABSPATH')) {
    exit; // Exit if accessed directly
}

class Nginx_Helper_Cache_Buster {

    public function __construct() {
        // Hook into plugin/theme update/install events
        add_action('upgrader_process_complete', array($this, 'clear_cache_after_update'), 10, 2);
        add_action('activated_plugin', array($this, 'clear_cache_after_plugin_activation'));
        add_action('deactivated_plugin', array($this, 'clear_cache_after_plugin_deactivation'));
        add_action('switch_theme', array($this, 'clear_cache_after_theme_change'));
    }

    /**
     * Clear Nginx Helper cache after plugin/theme updates
     */
    public function clear_cache_after_update($upgrader_object, $options) {
        if ($options['action'] == 'update' && 
            ($options['type'] == 'plugin' || $options['type'] == 'theme')) {
            $this->purge_nginx_cache();
        }
    }

    /**
     * Clear Nginx Helper cache after plugin activation
     */
    public function clear_cache_after_plugin_activation($plugin) {
        $this->purge_nginx_cache();
    }

    /**
     * Clear Nginx Helper cache after plugin deactivation
     */
    public function clear_cache_after_plugin_deactivation($plugin) {
        $this->purge_nginx_cache();
    }

    /**
     * Clear Nginx Helper cache after theme change
     */
    public function clear_cache_after_theme_change() {
        $this->purge_nginx_cache();
    }

    /**
     * Purge Nginx Helper cache
     */
    private function purge_nginx_cache() {
        if (function_exists('nginx_cache_purge')) {
            // Purge entire cache
            nginx_cache_purge();

            // Add admin notice
            add_action('admin_notices', array($this, 'show_purge_notice'));
        } else {
            // Nginx Helper plugin not active
            add_action('admin_notices', array($this, 'show_missing_plugin_notice'));
        }
    }

    /**
     * Show admin notice after cache purge
     */
    public function show_purge_notice() {
        echo '<div class="notice notice-success is-dismissible">';
        echo '<p>Nginx Helper cache has been automatically cleared due to plugin/theme changes.</p>';
        echo '</div>';
    }

    /**
     * Show admin notice if Nginx Helper is missing
     */
    public function show_missing_plugin_notice() {
        echo '<div class="notice notice-error is-dismissible">';
        echo '<p>Nginx Helper Cache Buster: The Nginx Helper plugin is not installed or activated. This plugin requires Nginx Helper to function.</p>';
        echo '</div>';
    }
}

// Initialize the plugin
new Nginx_Helper_Cache_Buster();
```

## Installation Instructions

1. Create a new folder in your WordPress plugins directory called `nginx-helper-cache-buster`
2. Create a file called `nginx-helper-cache-buster.php` inside that folder
3. Copy and paste the code above into that file
4. Go to your WordPress admin panel and activate the plugin

## Features

- Automatically clears Nginx Helper cache when:
  - A plugin is installed or updated
  - A plugin is activated or deactivated
  - A theme is installed or updated
  - The active theme is changed
- Shows admin notices when:
  - Cache is successfully cleared
  - Nginx Helper plugin is missing
- Lightweight with no external dependencies (except Nginx Helper)

## Requirements

- WordPress 4.6 or higher
- Nginx Helper plugin must be installed and activated

This plugin hooks into WordPress core actions related to plugin and theme management and triggers a full cache purge through the Nginx Helper plugin's API whenever these changes occur.

