# Responsive Sidebar Navigation with Next.js and Tailwind CSS

Here's a complete implementation of a responsive sidebar that transforms into a hamburger menu on mobile devices:

## Implementation

### 1. Create a new Next.js component (e.g., `Sidebar.js`)

```jsx
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import Link from 'next/link';

const Sidebar = () => {
  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false);
  const [isMobile, setIsMobile] = useState(false);

  useEffect(() => {
    const handleResize = () => {
      setIsMobile(window.innerWidth < 768); // Tailwind's 'md' breakpoint
      if (window.innerWidth >= 768) {
        setIsOpen(false); // Close sidebar when resizing to desktop
      }
    };

    // Set initial state
    handleResize();

    window.addEventListener('resize', handleResize);
    return () => window.removeEventListener('resize', handleResize);
  }, []);

  const toggleSidebar = () => {
    setIsOpen(!isOpen);
  };

  return (
    <>
      {/* Mobile Hamburger Button - only visible on mobile */}
      {isMobile && (
        <button
          onClick={toggleSidebar}
          className="md:hidden fixed top-4 left-4 z-50 p-2 rounded-md text-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-200 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-inset focus:ring-gray-500"
          aria-label="Toggle menu"
        >
          <svg
            className="h-6 w-6"
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            fill="none"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            stroke="currentColor"
          >
            <path
              strokeLinecap="round"
              strokeLinejoin="round"
              strokeWidth={2}
              d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h16"
            />
          </svg>
        </button>
      )}

      {/* Overlay - only visible when sidebar is open on mobile */}
      {isMobile && isOpen && (
        <div
          className="fixed inset-0 bg-black bg-opacity-50 z-40"
          onClick={toggleSidebar}
        />
      )}

      {/* Sidebar - always visible on desktop, conditionally visible on mobile */}
      <aside
        className={`bg-gray-800 text-white ${
          isMobile
            ? `fixed top-0 left-0 z-50 h-full w-64 transform transition-transform duration-300 ease-in-out ${
                isOpen ? 'translate-x-0' : '-translate-x-full'
              }`
            : 'hidden md:block md:w-64 md:min-h-screen md:fixed'
        }`}
      >
        <div className="p-4">
          <h2 className="text-xl font-bold mb-6">Navigation</h2>
          <nav>
            <ul className="space-y-2">
              <li>
                <Link href="/dashboard" legacyBehavior>
                  <a className="block px-4 py-2 hover:bg-gray-700 rounded transition">Dashboard</a>
                </Link>
              </li>
              <li>
                <Link href="/settings" legacyBehavior>
                  <a className="block px-4 py-2 hover:bg-gray-700 rounded transition">Settings</a>
                </Link>
              </li>
              <li>
                <Link href="/profile" legacyBehavior>
                  <a className="block px-4 py-2 hover:bg-gray-700 rounded transition">Profile</a>
                </Link>
              </li>
              <li>
                <Link href="/messages" legacyBehavior>
                  <a className="block px-4 py-2 hover:bg-gray-700 rounded transition">Messages</a>
                </Link>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </nav>
        </div>
      </aside>

      {/* Main content with padding adjustment based on sidebar */}
      <main
        className={`flex-1 ${
          !isMobile ? 'md:ml-64' : ''
        }`}
      >
        {/* Your page content goes here */}
      </main>
    </>
  );
};

export default Sidebar;
```

### 2. Usage in your layout file (`_app.js` or `layout.js`)

```jsx
import Sidebar from './Sidebar';

export default function Layout({ children }) {
  return (
    <div className="flex min-h-screen">
      <Sidebar />
      <div className="flex-1">
        {children}
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### 3. Optional: Add these styles to your globals.css

```css
@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@tailwind utilities;

/* Smooth transitions */
.transition-transform {
  transition-property: transform;
  transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
  transition-duration: 300ms;
}
```

## Features Implemented:

1. **Responsive Design**:
   - Always visible sidebar on desktop (width ≥ 768px)
   - Hidden sidebar on mobile with hamburger menu that slides in from left

2. **Mobile Menu**:
   - Hamburger icon appears only on mobile
   - Clicking it slides in the sidebar with animation
   - Overlay appears when sidebar is open

3. **Animations**:
   - Smooth slide-in/slide-out transition
   - Overlay with opacity for better UX

4. **Accessibility**:
   - Proper ARIA labeling
   - Semantic HTML elements

5. **State Management**:
   - Tracks mobile/desktop state
   - Tracks sidebar open/closed state
   - Automatically adjusts on window resize

The implementation uses only Tailwind CSS classes and Next.js features (no additional libraries required). The sidebar will automatically adapt between mobile and desktop views.

